    "result_text": "All 52 tests pass. The change is complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the disposable-domain email blocklist in `OwnerRestControllerV1.java`, following the existing Spring MVC validation idiom in the controller.\n\n**Changes** (`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`):\n\n1. Added a `DISPOSABLE_EMAIL_DOMAINS` constant holding the blocklist (`mailinator.com`, `tempmail.com`, `guerrillamail.com`).\n2. Extended `normalizeEmail(...)` so that after the existing syntactic check, it extracts the domain (part after `@`, compared case-insensitively since the value is already lower-cased) and throws `InvalidFieldsException(List.of(\"email\"))` when it's on the blocklist.\n\n`InvalidFieldsException` is already mapped to **400 Bad Request** by `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, so blocklisted domains are rejected with the required status. The check reuses the existing email-normalization path, so it applies to both `addOwner` and `updateOwner`.\n\n**Tests:** The full suite is green \u2014 `Tests run: 52, Failures: 0, Errors: 0`, including the new `Cp38Tests.errorRejectsDisposableDomain`.",
